    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεό-λῠτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>resolved in a new fashion,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Lyr.Adesp.</u>
					112
				</span></i>
			
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
				136
			</span></i> (prob. referring to the pyrrhic metre of the line, but perh.
			with a play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλος</span> 'limb', with
			ref. to Pentheus; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεόχυτος</span>).</div>
